  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.5,
      "text": "The whole life of a drop. The order matters."
    },
    {
      "t": 4.8,
      "text": "The facts are in a file, a name and a value each."
    },
    {
      "t": 10.3,
      "text": "Go straight at it and zep stops us. Nothing to stage into yet."
    },
    {
      "t": 15.8,
      "text": "So we create the drop first. Again, a nonce."
    },
    {
      "t": 21.3,
      "text": "Now the facts go in, one at a time."
    },
    {
      "t": 26.8,
      "text": "Same again for the second."
    },
    {
      "t": 32.3,
      "text": "Then we close it, passing the nonce along."
    },
    {
      "t": 37.8,
      "text": "Add anything now and it refuses."
    },
    {
      "t": 43.3,
      "text": "Sealed, anchored, both facts in."
    },
    {
      "t": 47.3,
      "text": "Everything has to go in before you close it."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Teaches that staging requires an existing drop, that the close needs the nonce, and that staging is refused after sealing."
}
